{"name":"Body language / presence training","deep":true,"image":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Body_Language_by_George_Welik.jpg/960px-Body_Language_by_George_Welik.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","credit":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Body_Language_by_George_Welik.jpg","caption":"Body Language by George Welik","source":"Wikimedia Commons"},"mentions":5,"casual":{"lead":["Training an open stance, steady eye contact and slower movement is meant to make you come across as more confident and commanding.","Wikipedia defines body language as nonverbal communication through posture, gestures, facial expressions, eye movement, touch and use of space. Power-posing research found a reliable effect on how people feel but not on hormones, and an unclear effect on behaviour. Gesture meanings also vary across cultures."],"sections":[{"h":"How people use it","paras":["People rehearse in front of a mirror or on video, work on pace, posture and eye contact in conversation, and combine it with grooming and posture work. Practice builds over weeks."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Risks & side effects","paras":["Low risk. Gestures and eye contact can be read differently across cultures."],"subs":[]}]},"gallery":[{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Body_Language_by_George_Welik.jpg/960px-Body_Language_by_George_Welik.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","full":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/6a/Body_Language_by_George_Welik.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","title":"Body Language by George Welik","license":"CC BY 2.0","creator":"Channel City Camera Club","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Body_Language_by_George_Welik.jpg","source":"Wikimedia Commons"},{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Yerevan%2C_Armenian_girls_posing_in_p