xing-mastering-body-language-voice-tonality-and-humor.739145/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20230920020206/https://looksmax.org/threads/the-ultimate-guide-to-charismamaxxing-mastering-body-language-voice-tonality-and-humor.739145/"},{"title":"social skills part 2 body language","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/social-skills-part-2-body-language.311988/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20220518155907/https://looksmax.org/threads/social-skills-part-2-body-language.311988/"},{"title":"mirroring body language is legit","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/mirroring-body-language-is-legit.105856/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20240615065126/https://looksmax.org/threads/mirroring-body-language-is-legit.105856/"},{"title":"More Trouble Than I Am Worth: Chaos Is The Plan (T3hPwnisher Log)","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/more-trouble-than-i-am-worth-chaos-is-the-plan-t3hpwnisher-log/276232","site":"T Nation · 8674 posts · 2021"},{"title":"Bad Ideas","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/bad-ideas/198222","site":"T Nation · 845 posts · 2014"},{"title":"600lb Deadlift Possible for Everyone?","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/600lb-deadlift-possible-for-everyone/224767","site":"T Nation · 825 posts · 2016"},{"title":"George W Bush Is A War Criminal","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/george-w-bush-is-a-war-criminal/42247","site":"T Nation · 213 posts · 2004"},{"title":"Fixing The Race Thing","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/fixing-the-race-thing/52368","site":"T Nation · 211 posts · 2005"},{"title":"Killing Babies No Different from Abortion","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/killing-babies-no-different-from-abortion/192518","site":"T Nation · 189 posts · 2013"},{"title":"Good Without God?","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/good-without-god/146250","site":"T Nation · 166 posts · 2010"},{"title":"Good News from Iraq","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/good-news-from-iraq/39947","site":"T Nation · 105 posts · 2004"},{"title":"FDA Authority Over Supplements","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/fda-authority-over-supplements/88288","site":"T Nation · 44 posts · 2007"},{"title":"Quitting Anti Depressants","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/quitting-anti-depressants/222596","site":"T Nation · 24 posts · 2016"},{"title":"Superhigh Megadosing CLA","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/superhigh-megadosing-cla/99137","site":"T Nation · 22 posts · 2008"},{"title":"Hacking the Election","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/hacking-the-election/224883","site":"T Nation · 20 posts · 2017"},{"title":"Kerry's Senate Record, Generally","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/kerrys-senate-record-generally/39871","site":"T Nation · 15 posts · 2004"},{"title":"Mosques Behaving Badly","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/mosques-behaving-badly/112662","site":"T Nation · 1 posts · 2008"}],"news":[],"social":[{"title":"The secrets of body language","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=5572558","site":"Hacker News","score":200,"comments":105,"year":2013},{"title":"How Studying Body Language Changed the Way I Socialize","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=4629317","site":"Hacker News","score":188,"comments":94,"year":2012},{"title":"Curving – Dog Body Language","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=20582954","site":"Hacker News","score":72,"comments":31,"year":2019},{"title":"Excellent body language resource","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=1080506","site":"Hacker News","score":73,"comments":24,"year":2010},{"title":"Self-driving cars learn to read the body language of people on the street","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=24322797","site":"Hacker News","score":24,"comments":71,"year":2020},{"title":"Emojis are the body language of the digital age","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=14709353","site":"Hacker News","score":43,"comments":48,"year":2017},{"title":"Body Language Reveals Wealth","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=476317","site":"Hacker News","score":32,"comments":30,"year":2009},{"title":"How to gain respect through body language","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=676585","site":"Hacker News","score":44,"comments":11,"year":2009},{"title":"Body Language and Machine Learning","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=24940154","site":"Hacker News","score":38,"comments":1,"year":2020},{"title":"A theoretical approach to body language and emotion","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=1428570","site":"Hacker News","score":22,"comments":2,"year":2010},{"title":"Body Language","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=4076553","site":"Hacker News","score":19,"comments":2,"year":2012},{"title":"Body Language Trainer (63 cards)","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=10097311","site":"Hacker News","score":17,"comments":3,"year":2015},{"title":"Gender and the body language of power","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=6391797","site":"Hacker News","score":8,"comments":3,"year":2013},{"title":"Best book on body language and just general cues?","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=8493559","site":"Hacker News","score":6,"comments":4,"year":2014}],"web":[{"title":"Body language - Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Body_language"},{"title":"Power posing - Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Power_posing"}]},"angle":{"goal":"Confidence & presence","chain":["Open stance, eye contact, slower pace","Calmer nonverbal signals","Appears more confident and commanding"],"effect":"indirect","text":"Open stance, steady eye contact and slower movement are practised to make you appear more confident and commanding, often alongside posture and grooming. Research supports increased felt confidence more than measured changes in how others judge the person."},"wikipedia":null,"grokipedia":null,"lead":["Body language or presence training is the deliberate practice of nonverbal behaviour, such as an open stance, steady eye contact and slower movements, intended to make a person appear more confident or commanding. It is discussed in appearance communities alongside posture and grooming.","Wikipedia defines body language as nonverbal communication through posture, gestures, facial expressions, eye movement, touch and use of space, mostly occurring without conscious awareness.[1] Research on whether trained postures change outcomes is contested: the \"power posing\" literature found a reliable effect on feelings but no reliable effect on hormones, and an unclear effect on behaviour.[2]"],"infobox":[["Category","Style meta"],["Practice","Open stance, eye contact, slower movements"],["Related topics","Posture awareness, power posing, kinesics"],["Research base","Nonverbal communication and power-posing studies"]],"sections":[{"h":"Description","paras":["The study of body movement in communication is called kinesics. Ray Birdwhistell, who developed it, held that gestures are polysemic and cannot be decoded in any absolute way, and rejected the term \"body language\".[1] Edward T. Hall introduced proxemics in 1966, defining intimate, personal, social and public distance zones.[1]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Elements practitioners emphasise","paras":["Reports note that leaning forward and nodding suggests openness, folded arms are often read as a closed mind, and relaxed hands suggest confidence.[1] Eye contact is often read as sincerity in workplaces, but meaning varies by culture, with prolonged gaze seen as a challenge or anger in some cultures.[1] The same gesture can differ in meaning: arms akimbo may signal relaxed confidence in Western countries but is considered rude in Bali.[1]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Power posing","paras":["In 2010 Dana Carney, Amy Cuddy and Andy Yap reported that holding expansive poses changed hormone levels in 42 participants, and Cuddy popularised the idea in a 2012 TED talk.[2] A 2015 replication by Eva Ranehill and colleagues found an effect on felt power but not on hormones, risk tolerance or behaviour.[2] Carney stated in 2016 that she no longer believed the effect was real, while Cuddy and colleagues published a 2018 meta-analysis of 55 studies reporting evidential value for effects on feelings.[2] A 2022 meta-analysis of 128 studies reported reliable effects on thoughts and feelings, no effect on physiological measures and an unclear behavioural effect, with few studies including a neutral-posture control.[2]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Limits of the research","paras":["Scholars disagree whether body language is universal, and Mehrabian's often-cited 7%-38%-55% split is widely debated.[1] Wikipedia states there is no scientific evidence that nonverbal cues reliably detect lies.[1]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Clinical studies","paras":["No studies found for presence training as a looks-related intervention. Related laboratory research on power posing is summarised above.[2]"],"subs":[]}],"lore":null,"timeline":[{"year":"1966","event":"Edward T. Hall introduces proxemics.[1]"},{"year":"2010","event":"Carney, Cuddy and Yap publish the original power-posing study.[2]"},{"year":"2015","event":"Ranehill and colleagues report a larger replication without hormone or behaviour effects.[2]"},{"year":"2016","event":"Carney states she no longer believes the effect is real.[2]"},{"year":"2022","event":"Körner and colleagues publish a 128-study meta-analysis.[2]"}],"refs":[{"title":"Body language","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Body_language","source":"Wikipedia","year":2026,"type":"encyclopedia"},{"title":"Power posing","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Power_posing","source":"Wikipedia","year":2026,"type":"encyclopedia"}],"studies":[{"title":"Power posing","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Power_posing","source":"Wikipedia","year":2026,"kind":null}],"reddit":[],"forums":[{"title":"How to differentiate between interest and indifference through body language","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/how-to-differentiate-between-interest-and-indifference-through-body-language.1561926/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20250912232033/https://looksmax.org/threads/how-to-differentiate-between-interest-and-indifference-through-body-language.1561926/"},{"title":"part 1 nt guide body language and abused dog theory","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/part-1-nt-guide-body-language-and-abused-dog-theory.992222/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20240527180335/https://looksmax.org/threads/part-1-nt-guide-body-language-and-abused-dog-theory.992222/"},{"title":"Guide THE ULTIMATE GUIDE TO CHARISMAMAXXING: MASTERING BODY LANGUAGE, VOICE TONALITY, AND HUMOR\n (2 Viewers)","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/the-ultimate-guide-to-charismamaxxing-mastering-body-language-voice-tonality-and-humor.739145/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20230920020206/https://looksmax.org/threads/the-ultimate-guide-to-charismamaxxing-mastering-body-language-voice-tonality-and-humor.739145/"},{"title":"social skills part 2 body language","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/social-skills-part-2-body-language.311988/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20220518155907/https://looksmax.org/threads/social-skills-part-2-body-language.311988/"},{"title":"mirroring body language is legit","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/mirroring-body-language-is-legit.105856/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20240615065126/https://looksmax.org/threads/mirroring-body-language-is-legit.105856/"},{"title":"More Trouble Than I Am Worth: Chaos Is The Plan (T3hPwnisher Log)","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/more-trouble-than-i-am-worth-chaos-is-the-plan-t3hpwnisher-log/276232","site":"T Nation · 8674 posts · 2021"},{"title":"Bad Ideas","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/bad-ideas/198222","site":"T Nation · 845 posts · 2014"},{"title":"600lb Deadlift Possible for Everyone?","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/600lb-deadlift-possible-for-everyone/224767","site":"T Nation · 825 posts · 2016"},{"title":"George W Bush Is A War Criminal","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/george-w-bush-is-a-war-criminal/42247","site":"T Nation · 213 posts · 2004"},{"title":"Fixing The Race Thing","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/fixing-the-race-thing/52368","site":"T Nation · 211 posts · 2005"},{"title":"Killing Babies No Different from Abortion","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/killing-babies-no-different-from-abortion/192518","site":"T Nation · 189 posts · 2013"}]}